    "updated_at": "2026-03-24T18:34:30Z",
    "body": "@mozfreddyb I don't want to get derailed by `is=...` since it's not ever going to be implemented by Webkit and I think likely will be deprecated. \n\nI brought it up because there is an attempt in the spec to make the serialization round trip successfully by sprouting the `is` attribute when it's not present. It's that behavior I don't think makes sense to try to replicate here since: (1) it's fairly unique and potentially  unexpected, (2) isn't removed when not in use so it doesn't really roundtrip, (3) would have to behave correctly with the subtree, which adds even more complexity.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
